# Architecture

Feature-first clean architecture for HOSSPI HMS frontend: `presentation → domain → data contracts`, with data implementations calling external services.

## Requirements

- Widgets must not call APIs, databases, secure storage, or sync services directly.
- Widgets must read display data only from Riverpod providers/controllers — no authoritative `setState` or server-data caches ([`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc)).
- Widgets must not store tokens or secrets.
- Repositories must not show dialogs, snackbars, or navigate.
- Data sources must not hold UI state; domain entities must not depend on widgets.
- `core` must not contain feature business rules; features expose intentional entry points.
- Use cases are required when decisions span multiple repositories.
- Mapping between DTOs, database models, and entities must be explicit.
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; internal IDs must not leak into UI or routes.
- Presentation must follow [`components.mdc`](./components.mdc) and [`layouts.mdc`](./layouts.mdc), localize all text, enforce RBAC+ABAC visibility ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)), and use design tokens only ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).

## Layer ownership

| Layer | Owns | Must not own |
|---|---|---|
| Presentation | pages, widgets, controllers, UI state | API, SQL, tokens |
| Domain | entities, contracts, use cases | JSON, widgets |
| Data | repos, DTOs, mappers, sources | navigation, UI messages |
| Core | cross-cutting infrastructure | feature rules |

